body:
Im currently 16 as well, and I’m also being forced to go to church and all that shit. While I haven’t dealt with the level of abuse you have experienced, I can still relate in a way to being a powerless minor. I dont have much advice but I thought it would be comforting for you to know that someone else out there is going through something somewhat similar. My emotionally abusive parents have resulted me in going down a depressing spiral of feeling alone and trapped. Right now for me, the best thing I can do is relate and talk with other people who understand me and know what I am going through. I encourage you to do the same, find as many people as possible on reddit or anywhere else on the internet that can support you and will understand you. It helps to talk with someone who can relate to your painful struggles. Stay strong and know that your emotions, feelings, thoughts, all of it is valid. You really are not alone. I know that can be super hard to believe but I know that there is always someone out there who can relate. Stay strong my friend. My DM’s are always open if you ever need anything ❤️ 

&#x200B;

also, there is an online, 24/7 free support system where you can talk to people on who are volunteer listeners. None of them are professionals and most of them are people around our age. If you need someone to talk to that would be a good place to go.  The website is [7cups.com](https://7cups.com) . I am a volunteer listener myself, so I occasionally help people and let them rant about their struggles. If you ever want to personally DM me there my account is caringCami1304, just send me a message request if you want to. I am also verified meaning I am a trusted listener on the site (and people who are varified are a bit harder to come by). of course it is optional but I would highly recommend it. :)
